{{Marvel Cinematic Universe Phases|tv=y}}
The [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] (MCU) television series are American [[Superhero fiction|superhero]] television shows produced by [[Marvel Studios]], based on characters that appear in publications by [[Marvel Comics]]. The series are set in the [[shared universe]] of the [[List of Marvel Cinematic Universe films|MCU film franchise]] and are released in the franchise's phases alongside the films.

The MCU first expanded to television after [[Marvel Television]] was formed in 2010, with that studio [[List of Marvel Cinematic Universe television series (Marvel Television)|producing numerous series]]. Marvel Television was shut down in December 2019 after Marvel Studios, the production studio behind the films, began developing its own series for the streaming service [[Disney+]]. Marvel Studios initially made its Disney+ series following a similar approach to its films, hiring [[head writer]]s to develop the series and directors to lead them during production. The early shows are mostly [[miniseries]] that focus on supporting characters from the films or introduce new characters that later appear in films. Animated series are produced under the [[Marvel Studios Animation]] division. 

Marvel Studios changed its television approach in 2022 and 2023, producing less content at the directive of parent company [[Disney]], hiring traditional [[showrunner]]s, and moving toward more multi-season series. In 2024, the studio began releasing series under the labels "Marvel Television", not to be confused with the earlier company, and "Marvel Animation". Some series use the "Marvel Spotlight" branding, which focuses on character-driven stories with less impact on the larger MCU narrative. Marvel Studios president [[Kevin Feige]] is an executive producer on every series, and Marvel Studios television and animation head [[Brad Winderbaum]] is an executive producer on most of them.

The first Marvel Studios series was ''[[WandaVision]]'' (2021) which is part of their [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Four|Phase Four]] slate along with ''[[The Falcon and the Winter Soldier]]'' (2021), the [[Loki season 1|first season]] of ''[[Loki (TV series)|Loki]]'' (2021), the [[What If...? season 1|first season]] of the animated ''[[What If...? (TV series)|What If...?]]'' (2021), ''[[Hawkeye (miniseries)|Hawkeye]]'' (2021), ''[[Moon Knight (miniseries)|Moon Knight]]'' (2022), ''[[Ms. Marvel (miniseries)|Ms. Marvel]]'' (2022), and ''[[She-Hulk: Attorney at Law]]'' (2022). [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Five|Phase Five]] includes ''[[Secret Invasion (miniseries)|Secret Invasion]]'' (2023), the [[Loki season 2|second season]] of ''Loki'' (2023), the [[What If...? season 2|second]] and [[What If...? season 3|third seasons]] of ''What If...?'' (2023–24), ''[[Echo (miniseries)|Echo]]'' (2024), ''[[Agatha All Along]]'' (2024), the [[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man season 1|first season]] of the animated ''[[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man]]'' (2025), the [[Daredevil: Born Again season 1|first season]] of ''[[Daredevil: Born Again]]'' (2025), and ''[[Ironheart (miniseries)|Ironheart]]'' (2025). [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Six|Phase Six]] features the animated ''[[Eyes of Wakanda]]'' (2025) and the [[Marvel Zombies season 1|first season]] of ''[[Marvel Zombies (TV series)|Marvel Zombies]]'' and its continuation special ''[[Marvel Zombies: The Winter Soldier]]'' (2025–27), ''[[Wonder Man (TV series)|Wonder Man]]'' (2026), the [[Daredevil: Born Again season 2|second]] and [[Daredevil: Born Again season 3|third seasons]] of ''Daredevil: Born Again'' (2026–27), ''[[VisionQuest]]'' (2026), and the [[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man season 2|second season]] of ''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man'' (2027). Phase Seven features the animated [[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man season 3|third]] and [[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man season 4|fourth seasons]] of ''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man'' and the specials ''[[Marvel Zombies: The Fist of Khonshu]]'' and ''[[Marvel Zombies: The Last Guardian]]'' (all 2028–29), and ''[[Zodiac (TV series)|Zodiac]]'' (2028)<!--, while other projects are in development for the future-->.

Additionally, several [[television special]]s have been released under the "[[Marvel's Special Presentation|Special Presentation]]" banners; the animated shorts series ''[[I Am Groot]]'' (2022–2023) was released across Phases Four and Five; and the animated series ''[[X-Men '97]]'' (2024–present) is being released as part of the MCU's [[Multiverse Saga]] storyline.
